($bc22299$life-money-bills-22$bc22299$,$bc22300$mutual_deflection$bc22300$,$bc22301$Case dismissed. The calendar says the first sentence for you.$bc22301$,$bc22302$$bc22302$,$bc22303$Each of you wants the other person to start because the first sentence can feel like volunteering to be the controlling one, the anxious one, or the person admitting a mistake. That mutual politeness is expensive when a small issue keeps compounding. Replace courage with a recurring appointment. At the same short weekly check, either person can add a yellow flag to the note before you meet. The calendar becomes the initiator, so neither partner has to manufacture a dramatic opening.$bc22303$,$bc22304$Add one factual yellow flag to the shared note before the next check, even if the numbers are incomplete. Open the scheduled check by reading the flag neutrally and asking what outcome would feel useful.$bc22304$,$bc22305$Case dismissed. The calendar says the first sentence for you.$bc22305$,$bc22306$Approved v4 template$bc22306$,$bc22307$Rename$bc22307$,$bc22308$$bc22308$,$bc22309$Add one factual yellow flag to the shared note before the next check, even if the numbers are incomplete.$bc22309$,$bc22310$Open the scheduled check by reading the flag neutrally and asking what outcome would feel useful.$bc22310$,$bc22311$Both of you save a recurring fifteen-minute Money Pulse with a shared yellow-flag note, fixed day, opener, task owner, and next check.$bc22311$,$bc22312$Case dismissed. The calendar says the first sentence for you.$bc22312$),
